    "problemStatement": "Consider an integer sequence BBB of length MMM. We define a few terms.\n\nA two-partition of BBB is an ordered pair of non-empty sets (S,T)(S, T)(S,T) satisfying the following conditions:\n\n\nS∪T={1,2,3,…,M}S\\cup T = \\{1, 2, 3, \\ldots, M\\}S∪T={1,2,3,…,M}\nS∩T=∅S\\cap T = \\emptysetS∩T=∅\nThe score of a two-partition P=(S,T)P = (S, T)P=(S,T) is defined as score(P):=min⁡i∈S(Bi)×max⁡j∈T(Bj)\\text{score}(P) := \\min_{i\\in S} (B_i) \\times \\max_{j\\in T} (B_j)score(P):=mini∈S​(Bi​)×maxj∈T​(Bj​).\n\nThat is, the score of a two-partition is the product of the smallest element among the indices of SSS, and the largest element among the indices of TTT.\n\nFinally, define f(B)f(B)f(B) to be the sum of scores of all two-partitions of BBB.\n\nYou are given an array AAA of length NNN.\n\nYour task is to process the following QQQ updates to it:\n\n\nGiven xxx and vvv, set AxA_xAx​ to vvv.\nOutput f(A)f(A)f(A) initially and also after each update.\n\nSince the values of f(A)f(A)f(A) can be large, compute them modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n†^\\dagger† A sequence bbb is a subsequence of an array aaa if bbb can be obtained from aaa by deleting some (possibly zero or all) elements.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and QQQ — the length of the array and the number of queries, respectively.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ — the initial values of the array.\nThe next QQQ lines describe the updates. The iii-th of these lines contains two space-separated integers xix_ixi​ and viv_ivi​, the parameters for the iii-th update.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nPrint Q+1Q+1Q+1 integers: the value of f(A)f(A)f(A) initially and after each update.",
